mediacodec: a decoder that stalls no longer holds its caller for ever

mediacodec_receive_frame loops while MediaCodec has no room for a packet and
no picture to give, without end. That is right while the decoder is busy. A
decoder that takes packets until it is full and never gives a picture leaves
the loop spinning for good: avcodec_send_packet never returns, the engine's
video thread never sees that its media was closed, the decoder is never
freed, and a window it was configured with stays connected to it, so nothing
else can draw there. The emulator's decoders do it for H.264 from MP4 or
Matroska and for HEVC from a transport stream; a device's decoder may do it
with a stream it should have refused.

With this the call fails after two seconds of that. The engine counts an
error and goes on, its thread can be closed, and the layer above sees a
decoder that gives no picture and has the media decoded in software
(AndroidPlayer.watchDecoder). The cost: a healthy decoder that stalls for
longer than two seconds has packets dropped until the next keyframe.

--- a/libavcodec/mediacodecdec.c
+++ b/libavcodec/mediacodecdec.c
@@ -491,6 +491,7 @@
     MediaCodecH264DecContext *s = avctx->priv_data;
     int ret;
     ssize_t index;
+    int stalled = 0;
 
     /* In delay_flush mode, wait until the user has released or rendered
        all retained frames. */
@@ -519,8 +520,23 @@
                  * return EAGAIN, which violate the design.
                  */
                 if (ff_AMediaCodec_infoTryAgainLater(s->ctx->codec, index) &&
-                    ret == AVERROR(EAGAIN))
+                    ret == AVERROR(EAGAIN)) {
+                    /* A decoder that takes no more packets and gives no
+                     * picture must not hold its caller for ever: some
+                     * devices' decoders do exactly that with a stream they
+                     * should have refused, and the caller then never gets
+                     * to close the decoder, nor to see that it was asked
+                     * to. Each round here waits for a picture for
+                     * OUTPUT_DEQUEUE_TIMEOUT_US, 8 ms: after two seconds of
+                     * them the call fails, and the packet in hand is kept
+                     * for the next one. */
+                    if (++stalled >= 250) {
+                        av_log(avctx, AV_LOG_WARNING,
+                               "MediaCodec has taken no packet and given no picture for two seconds\n");
+                        return AVERROR_EXTERNAL;
+                    }
                     continue;
+                }
                 return ret;
             }
             s->ctx->current_input_buffer = index;
